<!-- ============================================================
     Cisco Unified Communications Manager CVE-2026-20230 SSRF Detection Rules
     MITRE ATT&CK Techniques:
       T1190  - Exploit Public-Facing Application
       T1105  - Ingress Tool Transfer (file write via SSRF)
       T1083  - File and Directory Discovery
       T1059.004 - Command and Scripting Interpreter: Unix Shell
     Rule IDs: 103579-103588
     Author: SecOps Engineer
     Date: 2026-06-24
     CVE: CVE-2026-20230
     CVSS: 8.6 (HIGH)  - AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:N/I:H/A:N

     Vulnerability summary:
       Server-side request forgery (SSRF) in Cisco Unified Communications
       Manager (UCM) and UCM Session Management Edition (SME). Inadequate
       validation of HTTP requests allows an unauthenticated remote attacker
       to send crafted HTTP requests through the vulnerable component,
       potentially writing files to the system and escalating to root.
       Requires WebDialer service enabled (disabled by default).
       Actively exploited in the wild as of June 23, 2026.

     Affected products:
       - Cisco Unified Communications Manager (CUCM) all supported versions
       - Cisco Unified Communications Manager Session Management Edition (SME)
       Precondition: WebDialer service must be enabled

     Detection approach:
       1. HTTP request to WebDialer endpoint from external source (anchor)
       2. SSRF payload patterns  - internal IP references in WebDialer requests
       3. Burst of WebDialer probes (scanner / exploit framework fingerprint)
       4. File write events from Tomcat/UCM service user (post-SSRF file write)
       5. Unusual process spawn from Tomcat parent (post-exploitation RCE)
       6. Authentication-free WebDialer access (baseline for correlation)
       7. SSRF to localhost/metadata endpoints (cloud pivot or privilege esc)
       8. Correlated: external probe + file write within 5-minute window

     Severity tiers:
       Low (5)      - Base anchor (used for correlation; not standalone alert)
       Medium (9)   - Behavioral anomaly; investigate in context
       High (11-12) - Strong exploitation indicator; investigate promptly
       Critical (14-15) - Near-certain active exploitation; immediate response

     Log source prerequisites:
       - Cisco UCM Apache/Tomcat access logs forwarded to Wazuh manager
         (typically /var/log/active-cisco-ca/httpd/access_log or CiscoSSL log)
       - UCM system audit log (auditlog on UCM CLI)
       - Linux auditd on the UCM VM for file write and process exec events
       - Syslog forwarding from UCM to Wazuh via UDP/TCP 514
       - Process name anchor: "httpd" or "java" (Tomcat) in UCM log source

     References:
       - Cisco Advisory: cisco-sa-cucm-ssrf-cXPnHcW
       - NVD: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-20230
       - BleepingComputer: Cisco UCM CVE-2026-20230 exploited in attacks (2026-06-23)
     ============================================================ -->

<group name="cisco,cucm,ssrf,initial_access,cve_2026_20230,">

  <!-- ===========================================================
       T1190  - WebDialer HTTP request anchor
       Rule IDs: 103579
       Matches any HTTP request to the Cisco UCM WebDialer endpoint.
       Level 5 anchor used for correlation; not a standalone alert.
       The WebDialer endpoint is /ccmwebapi/WebDialerSrv or /webdialer/.
       =========================================================== -->

  <rule id="103579" level="5">
    <decoded_as>web-accesslog</decoded_as>
    <url type="pcre2">(?i)(/ccmwebapi/|/webdialer/|WebDialerSrv|/ccm/webdialer)</url>
    <description>Cisco UCM: HTTP request to WebDialer endpoint on $(hostname) -- CVE-2026-20230 attack surface; log source anchor for SSRF correlation (T1190)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1190</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>cucm_webdialer_access,</group>
  </rule>

  <!-- ===========================================================
       T1190  - SSRF payload in WebDialer request
       Rule IDs: 103580
       SSRF exploitation crafts HTTP request parameters containing
       internal IP addresses, localhost, or metadata service addresses.
       RFC1918 addresses or localhost in query parameters sent to
       WebDialer is a high-confidence SSRF indicator.
       =========================================================== -->

  <rule id="103580" level="13">
    <if_matched_sid>103579</if_matched_sid>
    <url type="pcre2">(?i)(127\.0\.0\.1|localhost|169\.254\.169\.254|10\.\d+\.\d+\.\d+|192\.168\.\d+\.\d+|172\.(1[6-9]|2\d|3[01])\.\d+\.\d+|::1|file://|dict://|gopher://|ftp://)</url>
    <description>Cisco UCM SSRF payload detected on $(hostname): WebDialer request contains internal address or SSRF protocol scheme -- active CVE-2026-20230 exploitation attempt (T1190)</description>
    <options>no_full_log</options>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1190</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>cucm_ssrf_payload,</group>
  </rule>

  <!-- ===========================================================
       T1190  - SSRF payload in request body/parameters (syslog variant)
       Rule IDs: 103581
       For environments where UCM logs appear via syslog rather than
       web-log decoder. Matches SSRF-indicative content in any
       Cisco UCM syslog message referencing WebDialer with internal
       address or redirect chaining patterns.
       =========================================================== -->

  <rule id="103581" level="12">
    <match type="pcre2">(?i)(webdialer|WebDialerSrv|ccmwebapi).*?(127\.0\.0\.1|localhost|169\.254\.169\.254|::1|file://|gopher://|dict://)</match>
    <description>Cisco UCM syslog SSRF indicator on $(hostname): WebDialer reference combined with internal address or protocol redirect -- CVE-2026-20230 exploitation signature (T1190)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1190</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>cucm_ssrf_syslog,</group>
  </rule>

  <!-- ===========================================================
       T1190  - WebDialer probe burst (scanner/exploit framework)
       Rule IDs: 103582
       Automated exploit tools and scanners generate high-frequency
       requests to the WebDialer endpoint during reconnaissance and
       exploitation. 10+ requests in 60 seconds from the same source
       is a reliable scanner fingerprint.
       =========================================================== -->

  <rule id="103582" level="11" frequency="10" timeframe="60">
    <if_matched_sid>103579</if_matched_sid>
    <same_srcip/>
    <description>Cisco UCM WebDialer burst on $(hostname): 10+ requests in 60 seconds from same source -- exploit scanner or automated CVE-2026-20230 exploitation tool (T1190)</description>
    <options>no_full_log</options>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1190</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>cucm_webdialer_burst,</group>
  </rule>

  <!-- ===========================================================
       T1190 / T1105  - File write from Tomcat/UCM service user
       Rule IDs: 103583
       Post-SSRF exploitation of CVE-2026-20230 allows an attacker
       to write files to the system. Auditd will show file creation
       by the tomcat or activemq process user (typically 'tomcat'
       or 'cisco' on UCM VMs) in unexpected filesystem paths.
       =========================================================== -->

  <rule id="103583" level="14">
    <if_group>audit,</if_group>
    <match type="pcre2">(?i)(type=CREATE|SYSCALL.*open.*O_CREAT|type=PATH.*nametype=CREATE)</match>
    <user type="pcre2">^(tomcat|cisco|ccmservice|ccmservice_user)$</user>
    <match type="pcre2">(?i)(/(tmp|var/tmp|home|opt/cisco|usr/local)/.*\.(sh|py|pl|rb|php|jsp|war|jar|class)|/etc/(cron|init\.d|rc\.d|passwd|shadow|sudoers)|/.ssh/)</match>
    <description>Cisco UCM service user file write in suspicious path on $(hostname): Tomcat/CCM service account created file in writable/sensitive directory -- potential CVE-2026-20230 post-SSRF file write leading to RCE (T1190, T1105)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1190</id>
      <id>T1105</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>cucm_file_write,</group>
  </rule>

  <!-- ===========================================================
       T1059.004 / T1190  - Unusual process spawn from Tomcat parent
       Rule IDs: 103584
       Following file write exploitation, attackers execute the dropped
       payload. Process execution with Tomcat (java) as parent process
       spawning shell interpreters or system utilities is post-exploitation.
       =========================================================== -->

  <rule id="103584" level="15">
    <if_group>audit,</if_group>
    <match type="pcre2">type=EXECVE|type=SYSCALL.*execve</match>
    <field name="ppid_name" type="pcre2">^(java|tomcat|ccmservice)$</field>
    <match type="pcre2">(?i)(/(bin|usr/bin|sbin)/(bash|sh|dash|zsh|python|perl|ruby|curl|wget|nc|ncat|socat|chmod|chown)|/tmp/)</match>
    <description>Cisco UCM: shell spawned from Tomcat/CCM service on $(hostname) -- java/tomcat executing shell or download utility is near-certain post-CVE-2026-20230 code execution; immediate incident response required (T1190, T1059.004)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1190</id>
      <id>T1059.004</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>cucm_rce,</group>
  </rule>

  <!-- ===========================================================
       T1083  - File/directory discovery after WebDialer auth bypass
       Rule IDs: 103585
       Attackers performing reconnaissance after gaining access via
       SSRF will enumerate directories. Path traversal sequences or
       directory listing commands in HTTP requests are lateral recon
       indicators when seen in WebDialer logs.
       =========================================================== -->

  <rule id="103585" level="11">
    <if_matched_sid>103579</if_matched_sid>
    <url type="pcre2">(?i)(\.\.\/|%2e%2e%2f|%252e%252e%252f|%c0%af|%c1%9c|\/etc\/|\/proc\/|\/sys\/|\/root\/|\/home\/)</url>
    <description>Cisco UCM WebDialer path traversal attempt on $(hostname): request contains directory traversal sequence -- potential CVE-2026-20230 filesystem reconnaissance (T1190, T1083)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1190</id>
      <id>T1083</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>cucm_path_traversal,</group>
  </rule>

  <!-- ===========================================================
       T1190 / T1105  - Correlated: probe burst + file write (5-min window)
       Rule IDs: 103586
       High-fidelity composite signal: WebDialer scan burst followed by
       a file write from the UCM service user within 5 minutes indicates
       a complete exploit chain  - reconnaissance, SSRF delivery, payload
       drop. This is a critical priority incident.
       =========================================================== -->

  <rule id="103586" level="15" frequency="2" timeframe="300">
    <if_matched_sid>103582</if_matched_sid>
    <if_matched_group>cucm_file_write,</if_matched_group>
    <description>Cisco UCM FULL EXPLOIT CHAIN on $(hostname): WebDialer burst followed by UCM service user file write within 5 minutes -- CVE-2026-20230 complete exploitation chain confirmed; CRITICAL incident response required (T1190, T1105)</description>
    <options>no_full_log</options>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1190</id>
      <id>T1105</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>cucm_exploit_chain,</group>
  </rule>

</group>
